---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import MockResponseGenerator from '../../components/MockResponseGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="API Mock Response Generator"
  description="Define a simple schema and instantly generate fake JSON data for testing — names, emails, UUIDs, dates, and more."
>
  <MockResponseGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why mock data instead of real data</h2>
  <p>
    Testing frontend components or API integrations against real production
    data is slow, risky, and often blocked by access controls. Fake data
    that matches your real schema lets you build and test UI, pagination,
    and edge cases without touching a real database.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this generator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Define your schema as <code>fieldName: type</code>, one per line.</li>
    <li>Supported types: string, name, email, number, boolean, uuid, date.</li>
    <li>Set how many records you want, then copy the generated JSON.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>API Mock Response FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Can I nest objects?</strong> Not yet — this generates flat
    objects. For nested structures, generate each part separately and
    combine manually.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Is this data really random?</strong> Yes, generated fresh each
    time from a fixed pool of sample names/words — click Regenerate for a
    new set.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
